From: PS4 Linux Baikal Port <noreply@ps4-linux>
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sdhci-pci: route Baikal IRQs through bpcie

Baikal's SDHCI function is behind the Sony southbridge interrupt fabric.
Allocating ordinary PCI MSI vectors bypasses that fabric, and removal must
free the vector through the same allocator that created it.

Source: https://github.com/rmuxnet/ps4-linux-12xx/commit/a827d7936c44e672138f269297965817f2e2a8f4
Adaptation: this target is Baikal-only, so no additional Kconfig symbol is
needed around the already device-ID-gated code.

---
diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-pci-core.c b/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-pci-core.c
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-pci-core.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-pci-core.c
@@ -346,11 +346,9 @@ static int aeolia_probe_slot(struct sdhci_pci_slot *slot)
 {
 	int err;
-	
-	if (slot->chip->pdev->device == PCI_DEVICE_ID_SONY_BAIKAL_SDHCI) {
-		err = pci_alloc_irq_vectors(slot->chip->pdev, 1, INT_MAX,
-			PCI_IRQ_MSIX | PCI_IRQ_MSI);
-	} else {	
+
+	if (slot->chip->pdev->device == PCI_DEVICE_ID_SONY_BAIKAL_SDHCI)
+		err = bpcie_assign_irqs(slot->chip->pdev, 1);
+	else
 		err = apcie_assign_irqs(slot->chip->pdev, 1);
-	}
-	
+
 	if (err <= 0) {
@@ -368,5 +364,8 @@ static int aeolia_probe_slot(struct sdhci_pci_slot *slot)
 
 static void aeolia_remove_slot(struct sdhci_pci_slot *slot, int dead)
 {
-	apcie_free_irqs(slot->chip->pdev->irq, 1);
+	if (slot->chip->pdev->device == PCI_DEVICE_ID_SONY_BAIKAL_SDHCI)
+		bpcie_free_irqs(slot->host->irq, 1);
+	else
+		apcie_free_irqs(slot->host->irq, 1);
 }
